{"t": 1795386409.011, "event": "terminal", "cmd": "systemctl --user enable --now svrngs.service; sleep 3; svrngs new house --as Sam --relay http://127.0.0.1:7900", "exit": 0, "answered": 0, "said": "Created symlink '/home/sam/.config/systemd/user/default.target.wants/svrngs.service' \u2192 '/etc/systemd/user/svrngs.service'.\nMade house, with you as Sam.\nSend this link to the people you want in it. It works for a day, while this computer is on:\n\n  <the link>\n\nhouse's folder is /home/sam/svrngs/house: what anyone in house puts there reaches this computer, and what you put there reaches theirs.\n"}
{"t": 1795386409.653, "event": "join", "said": "You're in house, as Alex.\nhouse's folder is /home/alex/svrngs/house: what anyone in house puts there reaches this computer, and what you put there reaches theirs."}
{"t": 1795386414.301, "event": "terminal", "cmd": "svrngs share 8101 --program llama-server --name coder --group house", "exit": 0, "answered": 2, "said": "People in your group can use all of coder that isn't kept back. Apps your friends open on their computers can only read it, unless you let them also send to it at /v1/embeddings; even then, each app sends only after the friend who opened it says yes. Let apps send? Type y, then press Enter: y\n\nIf coder takes a password on each request, paste what it takes in its Authorization header, then press Enter (Enter alone for none): \nYou lend coder (port 8101) to the groups you chose, as many at once as want it. To let fewer in at once, change it on your home page, or `svrngs share 8101 --group <group> --limit <number>`.\nLent coder: llama-server in ~/. svrngs checks port 8101 before each connection it carries there. While another program is on the port, it is closed. If the program starts again, coder closes until you approve what runs there: `svrngs approve coder`.\nThey cannot open /slots, /v1/stream, /v1/streams, /v1/chat/completions/control, /lora-adapters, /metrics, /tools, /cors-proxy, /models: svrngs keeps these back whenever a llama-server is lent, since they show one person's use of it to the others or change it for everyone.\nsvrngs is running here already, so they can open it now.\n`svrngs unshare coder` stops lending it.\n"}
