{"t": 1795386417.635, "event": "terminal", "cmd": "svrngs-keeper keep 8101 --lend coder", "exit": 0, "answered": 2, "said": "svrngs-keeper will run coder: llama-server with your model ~/models/qwen2.5-0.5b.gguf on port 8101, context 4096.\nIt starts with none of the settings your terminal added: DEBUGINFOD_IMA_CERT_PATH, DEBUGINFOD_URLS, EDITOR, LESSOPEN, LS_COLORS, MOTD_SHOWN, PATH, SELINUX_LEVEL_REQUESTED, SELINUX_ROLE_REQUESTED, SELINUX_USE_CURRENT_RANGE, SSH_CLIENT, SSH_CONNECTION, SSH_TTY, XDG_SESSION_CLASS, XDG_SESSION_ID, XDG_SESSION_TYPE.\nIt starts when you log in, and starts again if it stops (4 times a minute at most).\nThe llama-server you started stops, and this one takes its place. Keep it running? Type y, then press Enter: y\nsvrngs-keeper: enabled lingering for sam \u2014 the programs it keeps now survives logout and starts at boot without a login\ncoder runs here now, and it answers on port 8101: the systemd unit svrngs-keeper-coder.service.\nNow answering on coder's port: the systemd unit svrngs-keeper-coder.service (coder, kept by svrngs-keeper). Keep sharing coder with it? Type y, then press Enter: y\n\ncoder is kept to the systemd unit svrngs-keeper-coder.service (coder, kept by svrngs-keeper) now, and each time it starts again.\n"}
